{"id": "EUVD-2026-101215", "enisaUuid": "a739c13b-a3dc-35c9-b431-8cb359d093bc", "description": "OW2 ASM 3.0 before 9.11 contains a denial of service vulnerability that allows attackers to exhaust CPU by supplying crafted class files processed with ClassWriter.COMPUTE_FRAMES. Attackers can craft methods that make the unbounded MethodWriter.computeAllFrames() fix point algorithm converge slowly, tying up transforming threads for unbounded time.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:01:52", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/merge_requests/463", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/commit/ab68bbd2521359b7c8cd3517c6331ced3d817ed0", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/blob/ASM_9_10_1/asm/src/main/java/org/objectweb/asm/MethodWriter.java#L1595", "https://asm.ow2.io/versions.html", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ow2-asm-3.0-before-9.11-excessive-cpu-consumption-via-classwriter-compute-frames"], "aliases": ["GHSA-42q2-x6j4-w994", "CVE-2026-110261"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3f843488-5534-3c5e-b353-c1ef9a56d1f1", "product": {"name": "ASM", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}, "product_version": "3.0 <9.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3d1b8cca-c03c-30bc-9706-74552f53af3f", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}], "isExploited": false}